msgid "From files to documents in five minutes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Bring photographs, drawings and models into a study as documents, with* "
"Porta dentro."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A file on the disk is not yet part of a study. It becomes part of it when"
" the graph knows what the file is, which **document** it belongs to, when"
" that document was made and, for a model, which epoch it shows. EMStudio "
"does all of this in one window, *Porta dentro* (“bringing files in”, the "
"Italian name kept in every language, like Templu Mare). In this tutorial "
"you bring a few files into Templu Mare and find them in the study as one "
"document."
msgstr ""

msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You need a study open in EMStudio (the copy of Templu Mare from :doc"
":`first-study` is fine) and a few files that belong together: for example"
" three photographs of the same wall taken on the same day, or a drawing "
"and its scan."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bring the files in"
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose ``File ▸ Porta dentro…``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Desktop"
msgstr ""

msgid "The system's dialog opens: pick all the files at once and confirm."
msgstr ""

msgid "Web"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"EMStudio's own file picker opens, inside the page: pick one file and "
"confirm. To bring in several files, repeat the command for each file and "
"choose the same document every time."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The window **Porta dentro…** lists the files. Next to each name, EMStudio"
" says what the file is (a picture, a 3D model, a tileset, a drawing, a "
"GIS layer) and what it becomes in the study: a picture is **a file of the"
" document**, a model can be the representation of the place in an epoch."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Under **Document**, leave **New document** selected and write what the "
"document is in the field beside it, for example ``Photographs of the "
"north wall``. To add the files to a document the study already has, "
"choose it in the list instead."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fill **When was this document made?** with a year, a month or a day, for "
"example ``2015`` or ``2015-06``. The date is required: it is the date of "
"the document, which is often different from the date of what the document"
" shows."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the files are 3D models, choose in **Which epoch does it represent?** "
"the epoch the models show, and say in **When were the models acquired?** "
"when the survey was made. A reconstruction made in 2026 can represent the"
" II century A.D.: the two dates are kept apart."
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose a **Licence**, or leave **— as it is —**."
msgstr ""

msgid "Press **Porta dentro**."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A message confirms how many files came in and into which document. The "
"new document is a node of the graph, with its files, its date and its "
"licence."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the **Outliner**, the document is listed under **Documents**. Select "
"it, and the **Inspector** shows its fields."
msgstr ""

msgid "In the **Sources** workspace, the **Viewer & card** shows its files."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A model brought in as the representation of an epoch appears in the "
"**Space** workspace when that epoch is chosen."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The whole operation is one step of the history: ``Edit ▸ Undo`` takes it "
"all back."
msgstr ""

msgid "Other ways in"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``File ▸ Porta dentro…`` is one of several doors to the same window. You "
"also reach it by dropping a file on the **3D scene**, with the **+** in "
"the bar of the Space, and from a selection of files in the **Files** "
"window of the **Archive** workspace. A study file (an ``.em.json`` or a "
"GraphML) is not brought in this way: it opens as a graph."
msgstr ""

msgid "What next"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The how-to guides of :doc:`/how-to/bring-in/index` cover the other ways "
"material enters a study: a GraphML matrix, a table read through a "
"mapping, a folder of sources read by StratiMiner. :doc:`/how-to/sources"
"/declare-provenance` explains how to say where each file comes from."
msgstr ""

